2652d91bd8f4d1f9b00fe320c5f1071","name":"submit_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"checks\":{\"source_route_and_coverage\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"R001 is the sole source inference, with exactly H001–H004 as inputs and P as output. T001 maps S001–S008 to the same divided-power/basis, matrix-unit, arbitrary-lattice, reduction, and invariant-subspace route. T002 is an additional administrative conversion from the left scalar-extension view to the source tensor order, not a replacement proof route. The coarse T001 boundary is acceptable for this interface review: its statement is the actual terminal irreducibility proposition, while the explanation tracks each paragraph; no completed proof bodies are being assessed.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument\"},{\"document\":\"source-map.json\",\"pointer\":\"/direct_boundaries/R001\"},{\"document\":\"source-map.json\",\"pointer\":\"/source_outputs/P\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/terminal\"}]},\"parameters_and_allowed_inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Formal parameters preserve arbitrary M, K, p and integer lam; T001 binds the precise H001 prime, H002 characteristic, H003 interval, and H004 data predicate. D carries an arbitrary free Z-lattice basis and injective complex embedding rather than a standard lattice. D.H004 supplies the complex finite basis indexed by lam.toNat+1, highest-weight vector and relations, compatibility of integral operators with complex operators, and divided-power preservation; together these encode the source lattice/module conditions. The H003 guard makes the Nat conversion relevant only for nonnegative lam. Neither p=2 nor lam=0 is excluded. T002's sole internal input T001 is appropriate for a representation conversion and introduces no additional premise.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/inputs\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/parameters\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/premises\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/53-64\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/inputs\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/1/inputs\"}]},\"representations_and_conversion_obligations\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The source carrier is M ⊗[ℤ] K. T001 uses K ⊗[ℤ] M with the ordinary induced action; the proposal explicitly defines sourceTensorComm as a K-linear equivalence from the source order to this order. The sourceTensorModule instance transports scalar multiplication along the reverse commutor, and sourceTensorAction conjugates the induced action by that same reverse commutor. Thus the directions match: the equivalence sends source vectors to the T001 carrier, and it intertwines the three actions. T002 is the typed conditional conversion statement and its explanation requires transport of nontriviality and the invariant-subspace condition; this is more than a registry/comment assertion. The data record retains arbitrary-lattice identity and the needed basis/embedding and operator compatibility rather than substituting a standard representation. The representations are proposed and not proof-certified here, but the conversion is explicitly typed and internally planned.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/header\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion/type\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/7-38\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation_notes\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/1\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"}]},\"statements_and_local_plans\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The elaborated T001 signature is precisely conditional on prime p, CharP K p, 0≤lam<p, and D.H004, with conclusion LieIrreducible on K ⊗[ℤ] M and tensorAction of xM,yM,zM. LieIrreducible spells out nontriviality and every invariant K-subspace being bottom or top, matching the source definition using x,y,h (z is the formal name for h). T002 elaborates as implication from that exact T001 result to LieIrreducible on M ⊗[ℤ] K with sourceTensorAction; it quantifies the same ambient data and adds no mathematical assumptions. Its stated equivalence/action-intertwining plan follows from the definitions. T001's explanation covers the source paragraphs in their order, including the arbitrary localized-lattice rank-one step and the endpoints; it does not replace them by a library shortcut. These are interface and plan judgments only, not claims that any T proof body or final assembly has been completed.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/argument/0\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/argument/7\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/66-70\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/1\"}]}},\"findings\":[]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work 